  "rules": {
    "speech": "An utterance is one non empty TextGrid interval of one channel, 2 to 25 s long, with no <UNSURE> or <UNIN/> tag (no '<' at all), whose text contains at least one of the terms below (whole word, any case). All 44 doctor channel utterances that pass this filter are included. The 16 patient channel utterances were chosen by hand from the 35 that pass it, favouring rarer drugs; that choice is pinned here by list, not re-derived. Each clip runs from the interval's xmin minus 0.25 s to its xmax plus 0.25 s, at 16 kHz sample indices int((xmin - 0.25) * 16000) to int((xmax + 0.25) * 16000).",
    "gaps": "A gap is an empty interval of the doctor channel at least 3.5 s long, cut from xmin + 0.3 s to min(xmax - 0.3 s, xmin + 0.3 s + 8 s) with no padding. room_tone: the patient channel has no non empty interval overlapping the cut. other_party: it has one. The research run shuffled each kind with Python's random.seed(7) and kept the first 10 room_tone and the first 6 other_party gaps; that choice is pinned here by list.",
    "pad_seconds": 0.25,
    "gap_inset_seconds": 0.3,
    "gap_max_seconds": 8.0,
    "min_seconds": 2.0,
    "max_seconds": 25.0
